[B]Choose who joins from where, and send each player to their nearest server.[/B] InternetData checks each player's address as they join, refuses or flags to your staff the ones from countries and networks you don't want, and on a Velocity or BungeeCord network sends everyone else to the server you set for their continent or country.

[SIZE=5][B]🎯 What it does[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Refuses players from countries you don't want, or from any but the ones you list
[*]Keeps Tor and bots from rented servers off your server
[*]Tells your staff in chat, with the player's country, when someone joins over a privacy relay, a mobile network, satellite internet or an anycast address
[*]Sends each player to the server for their continent or country, on a Velocity or BungeeCord network
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]⚡ Up in a minute[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Put the jar in your server's plugins folder and restart
[*]Tor is blocked from the first join, with no account
[*]On a network, install it on the proxy alone: Velocity or BungeeCord sees each player once ([URL=https://github.com/internetdata/minecraft-plugin#getting-started]the README[/URL] has both)
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🔧 You decide what happens[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Block, alert your staff or allow, separately for VPNs, Tor, hosting networks, proxies, privacy relays, mobile networks, satellites and anycast
[*]Rules on any field of the answer, like one network or one country
[*]Your own kick and alert messages, with color codes
[*]A bypass list for players, addresses and ranges
[*]/inetd check looks up any player or address on the spot
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🎁 Free to start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]No account: countries, routing, Tor, privacy relays and anycast
[*]Free account, signed in with /inetd login: try VPNs, proxies, hosting networks, mobile networks and satellites too
[*]Paid plan: every check on every join, with the provider named in your messages
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🚀 Built for busy servers[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]One jar for Paper, Spigot, Purpur, Folia, Velocity and BungeeCord, on Java 17 or newer
[*]A login waits at most 2.5 seconds, and on a proxy the lookup runs while the player signs in
[*]If our API can't be reached, players are let in, unless you set it to refuse them
[*]Each answer is kept for an hour, so a player who rejoins costs no second lookup
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]🔒 What it sends[/B][/SIZE]
For each player who joins, the plugin sends their address to api.internetdata.io and nothing else about them: no name, no UUID. Requests name the plugin, its version and your server software. [URL=https://internetdata.io/privacy]Privacy policy[/URL]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Setup and help[/B][/SIZE]
Every setting, command and rule: [URL=https://docs.internetdata.io/integrations/minecraft]docs.internetdata.io/integrations/minecraft[/URL]. The source: [URL=https://github.com/internetdata/minecraft-plugin]GitHub[/URL]. Questions: support@internetdata.io
